The [enum](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:68) and [setup assertions](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_re_width_probe.py:491) establish this.

Several claims are **OVERSTATED**.

- **�?oPass 2 found one �?� pass 3 found four more.�??**  
  Correct as a description of the *repair that was adopted*, but misleading as discovery history. Grok�?Ts pass-2 answer already names bits **6, 8, 9, 10**, exactly as A2 later acknowledges. More importantly, the pass-3 brief itself supplies: �?oBits 6, 7, 9, 10 are swept by nothing.�?? The packet-fed respondents adjudicated that supplied premise; they did not independently discover all four from source. [Pass-2 grok:55](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/_scratchpad/panel_sgirekills_pass2_20260908/grok.txt:55), [PASS3_brief.md:102](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/sgirekills/PASS3_brief.md:102).

- **B2: �?oEIGHT sites�??; �?onine return-value sites�??; �?oeight precedents.�??**  
  **Eight textual matches is correct.** Two are disabled: the assignments at lines **356** and **383** are inside `#if 0`. There are **six active V0 assignment sites**, including one PROM site; five are active PAL cases. Including `swpctx` gives seven active assignment sites in this census. The diagnosis survives, but �?oeight precedents�?? obscures that distinction. [Disabled blocks](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_alpha_palcode.c:349).

- **B1: �?oThey are now verified,�?? used to advance the severity/ordering argument.**  
