 118: 
 119:   The dispatch transcription is correct: the wrapper passes `(-2, 0)`, `a0` is unsigned, the comparison selects VADDR, and ordinary 64-bit initialization supplies the all-ones mask. The precise consequence is **only cached page-zero entries are selected; if none exist, nothing is invalidated**. Other cached address mappings on that CPU survive this call. [Wrapper:281](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/alpha_cpu.h:281), [dispatch:321](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_alpha_palcode.c:321), [mask:140](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu.c:140), [selection:1241](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c:1241).
