 122:   Bit 9 belongs to `draw_primitive`; bit 10 belongs to the shared pixel helper, also called by **`do_mte_transfer`**. "Drawing-engine path" needs that qualification if it means the DE primitive path specifically. [MTE calls:1530](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1530).
 123: 
 124: - **B3: the default arm "fills a buffer with random() and writes it."**  
 125:   It assigns **four bytes of an eight-byte buffer**. The transfer length is `bufdepth`, whose domain includes eight. The narrower account matters because this is exactly where the separate uninitialized-buffer issue overlaps. The `16 - 4 = 12` mode count and the documented YCRCB value are correct. [Buffer and default:307](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:307).
