  20: REASONED, primary edit: replace the test with the operator's low-bit stream decode - `if (a0 & 3)`  VADDR, else ALL, ideally dressed as `switch (a0 & 3) { case 1: /* I */ case 2: /* D */ case 3: /* I+D */ .VADDR.; default: ALL }` with a comment citing the architectural encoding. It *looks like an upgrade* - it implements stream selectivity and handles 1/2/3 exactly right - but `0xff.fe & 3 = 2` and `0xff.ff & 3 = 3`, so TBIA and TBIAP both land in VADDR(a1=0): the identical defect, wearing a spec citation. Secondary: `if (a0 >= 1 && a0 != (uint64_t)-1)` - "explicitly special-case TBIAP" - fixes TBIAP, leaves TBIA broken, and defeats any witness that exercises only TBIAP.
