{"id": "lcaconfbus1kill", "sev": "high", "state": "open", "opened": "2026-09-07", "title": "dev_lca.c: writing 0x1 to LCA_IOC_CONF is ACCEPTED by its guard and arms a host kill in lca_pci_conf -- `bus != 0` is a bare fatal()+exit(1) five lines below the file's own graceful-degradation precedent", "commits": "41923ac"}
hold_question: Four seats independently established that NO row can separate IMPLEMENT from an explicit all-ones DECLINE here, because an empty bus 1 answers all-ones under both and nothing in this tree places a device on bus 1.  Should the round (a) ship the fix with a detector that provably cannot discriminate it, disclosing that under clause (e); or (b) ADD a synthetic bus-1 device to the test apparatus so the row becomes possible -- an addition to the harness made in order to observe a fix, which is the shape the addition licence exists to police?
state_note: FILED 2026-09-07.  Surfaced while verifying a claim in the grok seat's `lcabadval` pass-1 BODY (its
verdict line did not carry it) -- and **verified to be sharper than the seat stated it**, by opening
both functions.

**THE DEFECT: an ACCEPTED write to one register arms a host kill in a DIFFERENT function.**

`DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc)`, `case LCA_IOC_CONF`:

    d->ioc_conf = idata;
    /*  Only bit 0 is implemented so far, the PCI bus 0 vs
        bus non-0 selection bit.  */
    if (idata & ~1) {
            fatal("TODO: Write to unimplemented bit of IOC_CONF: 0x%" PRIx64 "\n", ...);
            exit(1);
    }

**`0x1` PASSES that guard.**  `idata & ~1` is 0, so the write is accepted, stored, and the arm's own
comment describes bit 0 as the implemented selector.

`DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_pci_conf)` then consumes it:

    bus = d->ioc_conf & 1;
    if (bus == 0) {
            for (dev=0; dev<21; dev++)
                    if (tag & (0x800 << dev))
                            break;
            if (dev >= 21) {
                    /*  fatal("[ LCA: No bus 0 device? TODO ]\n");
                    exit(1);  */
                    dev = 0;
            }
    } else {
            fatal("TODO. Non-zero bus.\n");
            exit(1);
    }

So: **guest writes 1 to IOC_CONF (accepted), then performs any PCI configuration-space access, and
the host process exits.**  Two guest accesses, both to registers the model implements, neither of
them rejected.

*** WHY IT IS ITS OWN ROW AND NOT PART OF [[lcabadval]]. ***  Every kill `lcabadval` covers is a
guard REFUSING a value it does not recognis
