state_note "s project\nnamed after `panel.sh`'s phantom re-fire.\n\n**LAUNCHER DEFECT 2: the script exited 0 while holding `rc=1`.**  It captured codex's status into a\nvariable, printed it, and then ended on a successful command.  **The harness reported the task\nCOMPLETED.**  That is the failure-laundered-into-a-clean-completion class, a"
state_note ' grok harness review against `cpu_alpha_instr.c` -- so a guest `stq`\ndelivers `len = 8` and `idata` holds bit 32.  **The discriminating store is therefore\n`0x100000000` to `k0(0x180000020)`: the guard `idata & ~1` fires, and `(int)idata` prints `0x0` --\na value that same guard ACCEPTS.**\n\n> **THE CONTROL THIS WITNESS OWES,'
state_note ' proves the arm fired and that a 32-bit zero store could not\n> have produced that pair.\n\n**Q3 CONFIRMED IN DETAIL, and it hardens S2:** `stq` is opcode `0x2d` -> `loadstore_type 3` -> `LS_Q`;\n`host_store` is NULL for a device page, so it falls to `LS_GENERIC_N` and calls `memory_rw(..., 8,\nMEM_WRITE)`; the memblock granul'
state_note "00000000 == 0` is IMPLEMENTATION-DEFINED, not guaranteed by C99.\nGCC/Clang truncate, so the witness holds on this build -- but the row should not claim a language\nguarantee.\n\n*** AND THE 309 FIGURE WAS ALREADY IN THIS ROW'S OWN ENTRY, DATED 2026-08-31. ***  I ran a census\ntoday, got 226, treated it as new, and was correcte"
