state_note ' counting only the four handled types; 7 of 20 including YCRCB.)\n\n**GET -- uninitialised bytes consumed by the recombination: 30 of 64.**\n\n## TWO OF MY PREMISES WERE WRONG\n\n* **`random()` INITIALISES its four bytes.**  So the `sgirandomcolour` arm does NOT leak\n  uninitialised data -- it writes objectionable data.  Differ'
state_note 't paths\n\n    uint8_t buf[8] = {0};\n\n*"It preserves the output of otherwise defined paths whose consumed bytes were already initialised.\nPUT overwrites the same bytes before transferring them; GET overwrites the requested bytes before\nrecombination.  Transfer addresses and lengths remain unchanged."*  **That is the Q4 prop'
