state_note 'nce judgment, not a claim that it has the greatest potential\nseverity"* -- which is the rung-versus-severity distinction the ladder already insists on, arrived at\nindependently.\n\n*** AND IT REFUTED A GROUPING HYPOTHESIS I HAD FLOATED: "the claim that `alphapteprot` prevents all\nguest paging is not established by this review'
state_note 'Alpha row.  THE CLUSTER IS NOW FULLY ASSESSED. ***\n\n**THE CLAIM IS TRUE BUT NARROWER THAN FILED: it holds for kernel mode with PTBR == 0 on that exact\nVA.**  There are TWO hits on `0xfffffffd80000000` in `memory_alpha.c` and **only one terminates**;\nthe other is a bare `fatal("AYONA3\n")` -- a debug string left in the tree.'
state_note '\n")` -- a debug string left in the tree.  `fatal()` only prints;\nthe termination is the `exit(1)` immediately after, with nothing recovering in between.\n\n## THE CENSUS I ASKED FOR, and it changes the framing\n\n| walker | unmodelled / stub region | ordinary translation miss |\n|---|---|---|\n| Alpha | this one VA: `fatal`+`ex'
