TITLE 'dev_sgi_re.c horrible_getputpixel(): uint8_t buf[8] is never initialised and the guest picks how many of its bytes are used -- uninitialised host stack reaches guest-visible memory on PUT and *color on GET'
note START ''
state_note START "FILED 2026-09-07, found while writing the design brief for `sgirandomcolour' -- i.e. by reading the arm NEXT\nto the one grok pointed at.  **This is a bigger defect than the row that led me to it, and it needs no\nundocumented mode at all.**\n\n`horrible_getputpixel()' declares `uint8_t buf[8];' and NEVER INITIALISES IT.  Verified: no memset in the\nfunction, no initialiser, and the only memsets in the file are the device struct, `rop_used' and `zerobuf'.\nThe two fields that decide how much of `buf' is USED are decoded from the SAME guest-written mode register\nand are INDEPENDENT of each other:\n\n    uint32_t color_mode = mode & DE_MODE_TYPE_MASK;      /* bits 4-7  */\n    int bufdepth = 1 << ((mode >> 8) & 3);               /* bits 8-9  -> 1, 2, "
state_note "a stack OVERFLOW.  **It did not ask what fills the\nbytes it had just added.**  The array is the right size and the contents are undefined.\n\nSEVERITY: guest-reachable read of uninitialised host stack whose value becomes guest-visible.  In a loop the\nstale bytes are usually the PREVIOUS pixel's, so the everyday symptom is wrong colours; on the first call in\na frame they are whatever the host stack held.  Both mode words are ordinary device registers reached by\nordinary stores, and all seven call sites pass one of them.\n\nNOT YET WITNESSED -- "
state_note 'al-adjudication rule says a ruling short of the roster is provisional on its face, so they wait for\nthe full six.\n\n*** PASS-1 BRIEF DEFECT, RAISED INDEPENDENTLY BY ALL THREE PACKET-FED SEATS: I ASSERTED A PREMISE THEY\nCOULD NOT CHECK, AND SAID `SETTLED PREMISES: NONE CARRIED\'. ***\n\nNo burns -- all three returned real verdicts on a 31 KB brief -- and all three named the same hole:\n  * **minimax**: *"the load-bearing premise is NOT CHECKABLE and the brief states it confidently anyway ...\n    That single fact -- the body of `cpus/memory_rw.c\' '
state_note 'ers can\nsee, whose blind spots are nested-comma argument lists and cast buffer arguments"*.  The two new correctness\nfindings the same seat raised are filed separately as [[sgirergbroundtrip]] and [[sgimtedepth4dead]].\n\n*** PASS-1 ADJUDICATION.  EVIDENCE BASIS: 6 of 9 -- six scriptable seats ANSWERED (0 walled, 0 down, 0\nburns, novelty 93-100%); agy DELIBERATELY NOT FIRED on the measurement reserve; opus5 and fable5 HELD for the\n2026-09-09 adjudication by standing owner directive.  The three absences are DIRECTED, not failures -- but the\npr'
state_note '-691\'.  **I asked the panel not to let the convenience of one round drive the\nanswer, and it did not.**  ACCEPTED: two rounds.\n\n**D2 -- Q5, SEVERITY: grok says MEDIUM, kimi says HIGH *conditionally*.  RESOLVED BY KIMI\'S CONDITION, not by\ncounting.**  kimi: HIGH is defensible for this fork\'s mandate *\'provided the entry carries the corrected\nreachability framing ... Do not ship the entry with "no undocumented value anywhere" in it.\'*  The row KEEPS\nHIGH and the framing is corrected here.  grok\'s MEDIUM rests on disclosure impact, which is g'
state_note 'LL SITES TAKE THE GUEST MODE WORDS** -- *"the two MTE sites construct their own modes"*.\nMy reachability paragraph implies all seven.\n\n**7. SEVERITY: MED, not HIGH.**  *"HIGH is not established by inheriting #95\'s severity."*  And it refuses\nthe downgrade too: *"\'usually the previous pixel\' and \'first call in a frame\' are unsupported explanations of\nstack contents.  They cannot justify downgrading this to a cosmetic rendering defect."*  **Both of my\nseverity arguments were unsupported, in opposite directions.**  Lowered to MED provisionall'
