TITLE 'cpu_alpha_palcode.c swpctx returns the old context in a0 while the ABI wrapper in alpha_cpu.h reads it from v0'
note START ''
state_note START 'FILED 2026-09-07 from the codex reachability pass (regress/artifacts/alphapfnoffset/codex_reachability_20260907.txt), raised under the\nfound-something-else licence on a brief about something unrelated.\n\ncodex: *"`swpctx` writes the old context into **a0**, although the supplied ABI wrapper returns **v0**.\nThis independently contradicts the handler\'s contract."*\n\nIf correct, a guest calling the PALcode `swpctx` gets its previous context pointer in the wrong register --\nthe caller reads `v0` and finds whatever was there.  That is a silent wrong value rather than a crash, which\nis the harder kind to notice.\n\n*(SUPERSEDED WITHIN THE HOUR, kept because the record should show the order.  This paragraph read:\n**"NOT VERIFIED BY ME.  Both citations'
