state_note 'value), and it labelled that *"a confidence judgment, not a claim that it has the greatest potential\nseverity"* -- which is the rung-versus-severity distinction the ladder already insists on, arrived at\nindependently.\n\n*** AND IT REFUTED A GROUPING HYPOTHESIS I HAD FLOATED: "the claim that `alphapteprot` prevents all\nguest paging is not established by this review." ***  I had suggested the page-walk row might be a\nprerequisite for testing the others; that is not supported, and scheduling on it would have been\nscheduling on an assumption.  '
