  37: The unwritten elements are **uninitialised on every invocation**, including the first. Reused stack storage can physically contain bytes from an earlier call-or unrelated earlier work-but there is no persistent previous-call buffer in the language semantics. Automatic storage becomes indeterminate again on each execution of the declaration. [C11 draft, 6.2.4 and 6.7.9](https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg14/www/docs/n1570.pdf)
