1807: ### 7g-3. (MED) IS A **CODE-INTENT WARRANT** ENOUGH TO CHANGE GUEST-VISIBLE OUTPUT?
1808: 
1809: Raised by the minimax seat and confirmed by me: **there is no SGI/CRIME hardware documentation in
1810: this project.** Derived, not assumed \u2014 `ls _scratchpad/*.pdf` lists sixteen manuals (ARM, MIPS,
1811: m88k, SH, PowerPC, DC21285, i8254, MVME187) and **none for this device**.
1812: 
1813: So the fix picks `DE_MODE_TYPE_RGBA` on two internal warrants only: the dead branch itself named
1814: RGBA, and the comment says *"copy 32 bits"* while the RGB arm zero-pads the low byte and therefore
1815: does not copy 32 bits of data. minimax put the gap precisely: *"no CRIME/MTE hardware spec is
1816: cited. A regression that picked RGB instead would still pass the witness."* (That specific escape
1817: is now closed by `fill bot`/`copy 4th` \u2014 but the WARRANT question survives the closure.)
1818: 
1819: > **Is "the dead code\'s own choice, plus a comment" a sufficient warrant for a round that changes
1820: > what a guest reads back?** This round says yes and discloses the basis. The alternative
1821: > disposition would be to fix the UNREACHABILITY (make the branch live) while filing the TYPE
1822: > choice separately \u2014 which nobody proposed and which I do not think is better, but I have not
1823: > tested that opinion against a seat.
1824: 
1825: ---
